WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.970
-The President's ex-campaign
chairman has flipped on him

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.272
and his Supreme Court nominee
has been imperiled

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.074
by a serious
sexual-assault allegation.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.343
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:15.214
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.517
-One by one,
Trump's closest aides

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:20.319
have turned on him and struck
plea deals with prosecutors.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:23.489
But there was one, who,
for months, refused to cave,

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.958
and that was his ex-campaign
chairman, Paul Manafort.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:27.927
Manafort went all the way
to trial.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.662
And to ensure
Manafort's loyalty,

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.430
Trump repeatedly praised him.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.667
-I think the whole
Manafort trial is very sad

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.335
when you look
at what's going on there.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:39.405
I think it's a very sad day
for our country.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.874
He worked for me for
a very short period of time.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:42.942
But you know what?

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.578
He happens to be
a very good person.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.079
Paul Manafort's a good man.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.148
He was with Ronald Reagan.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:52.184
He was with a lot of different
people over the years,

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:55.855
and I feel very sad about that.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.357
It doesn't involve me,
but I still feel --

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:00.593
You know, it's a very sad thing
that happened.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.663
This has nothing to do
with Russian collusion.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.032
-I like how Trump
tries to praise Manafort,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.034
but his instinct for
self-preservation

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.103
keeps leaking through.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.972
"Paul is a very good friend,
whom I barely know,

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.041
and his crimes
had nothing to do with me,

00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:17.310
his very good friend."

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.544
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.381
Also, do you only
give interviews on tarmacs now?

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.515
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.384
Trump's strategy
for dealing with reporters

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.553
is to always be near something
louder than him.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.490
"Mr. President, why is everyone
around you a criminal?"

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.291
"I'm sorry!
You'll have to speak up!

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.859
I'm making wood chips!"

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:39.064
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:42.268
Gonna catch on soon
with Sarah Sanders.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.603
She's gonna
give press conferences

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.104
while making daiquiris.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.572
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:50.309
"That is not something I've
spoken to the President about."

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:51.544
[ Imitates blender
motor whirring ]

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.145
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:55.381
So there you go --
Trump heaped praise on Manafort,

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.449
calling him a brave
and wonderful man

00:01:57.449 --> 00:02:00.053
who would,
under no circumstances, flip.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.088
-Paul Manafort has flipped.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.557
-During an hour-long hearing
in federal court,

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:07.393
Manafort pleaded guilty
to two felony counts

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.362
related to his foreign lobbying.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:12.364
Even more significantly,
he agreed to cooperate

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:14.066
in Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:17.637
Russia investigation by
providing unspecified documents

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.072
and testifying
before the grand jury.

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:22.641
-Wow!
Your friend just flipped on you.

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:24.143
What do you say to that?

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:25.244
[ Engine whirring loudly ]

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.680
I said your friend
just flipped on you!

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.082
What do you --
Never mind.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:32.718
[ Laughter and applause ]
Pointless.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:37.122
Pointless.

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:39.225
And Manafort didn't just
have to plead guilty

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.426
and agree to cooperate.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.561
He also had to give up
his lavish lifestyle,

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:43.630
including an apartment

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.865
in Donald Trump's
most famous building.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.868
-As part of his punishment,
Manafort agreed to forfeit

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.471
bank accounts, life insurance,
and several properties,

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.541
including his apartment
in Trump Tower.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.543
-You know what
the best burn would be?

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.078
The best burn would be

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.613
if Robert Mueller
took the apartment.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.648
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:06.452
If Mueller moved in, he would be
the kind of tenant Trump hates.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.921
"Hey, the guy in 4C went through
the recycling again.

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:10.489
He says your mixing your paper
and your plastic."

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.058
"I hate that guy so much."

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.027
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.728
For the prosecution,
there was maybe no one

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.229
more valuable than Manafort.

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.898
He knows as much about what
happened in 2016 as anyone.

00:03:19.898 --> 00:03:21.300
For example,
he was actually in

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.735
that infamous
Trump Tower meeting

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.470
with the Russians in 2016.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.906
And he seems to know
a lot about Trump's finances

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.307
and connections to Russians.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:32.312
As you can tell from this clip,
from the 2016 campaign,

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:35.014
which is truly
one of our favorites.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:38.284
-So to be clear, Mr. Trump
has no financial relationships

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.252
with any Russian oligarchs?

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:42.755
-That's what he said.
I -- I -- That's what I said.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.457
That's obviously what the --
our position is.

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.961
-How was that guy a successful
criminal for so long?!

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.362
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:51.564
I mean, that was one.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.933
He got one question
about Trump's finances,

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.134
and he broke down

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.835
like a malfunctioning
Chuck E. Cheese robot.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.137
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.505
"Uh, that --
that's what he said.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.106
That's -- That --
That's what he --

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:03.209
That's what I --
Happy birthday to yo--

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.612
Ha-Ha-Ha-Happy birth--
Buh-uuh-buuh!"

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:09.649
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.984
"Mom, the mouse is smoking!"

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:14.387
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.189
So, for months now, the screws
have been tightening on Trump,

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.525
but he seemed to have
one last ace in the hole --

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.327
his Supreme Court nominee,
Brett Kavanaugh.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.995
If Kavanaugh makes it
onto the court,

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:26.164
he could very well rule
on key aspects of Trump's case.

00:04:26.164 --> 00:04:28.367
And Kavanaugh has been a loyal,
partisan Republican

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.202
whose views on executive power

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:32.038
could not be friendlier
to Trump.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.372
Throughout
his confirmation hearings,

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.875
Kavanaugh has refused to take
positions on legal issues

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.044
that could be crucial
to Trump's survival.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:41.747
-Trump claims he has an absolute
right to pardon himself.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.050
Does he?

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.621
-The question of self-pardons is
something I've never analyzed.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.323
-Can a sitting President

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:53.458
be required to respond
to a subpoena?

00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:56.228
-So that's
a hypothetical question.

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:59.932
-Should a president
use his or her authority

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.969
to pressure executive
or independent agency officials

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:06.338
into carrying out directives
for purely political purposes?

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:09.575
-I need to stay
not just away from the line

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.210
but three ZIP codes away
from the line

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.312
of current events or politics.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:14.780
-Hey, you don't get to stay

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.816
three ZIP codes away
from Donald Trump.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.684
Some of us
are entire states away

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:19.785
and we can still hear him

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.454
screaming over the sound
of a jet engine.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.289
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.691
Also, nothing says
you're not from New York

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:29.061
more than thinking three ZIP
codes away is a large distance.

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:30.462
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:33.466
In New York, three ZIP codes
is like two Starbucks away.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.669
Now, when this process started,

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.838
it seemed to many like Kavanaugh
would sail through,

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.506
given that Republicans
control the Senate.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.742
But then, last week,
Senate Democrats disclosed

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.177
that they had referred
a complaint regarding Kavanaugh

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:46.713
to the FBI
for investigation.

00:05:59.024 --> 00:06:00.226
Kavanaugh denied it,

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:02.862
and Republicans responded
by rushing to defend him.

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:05.030
-65 women stepping forward
to defend

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.567
President Trump's Supreme Court
nominee Brett Kavanaugh.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.401
-Right after we saw
these allegations came out,

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:12.972
we heard from 65 women
defending him in a letter

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:15.107
to Senate Judiciary Committee
Chair Chuck Grassley

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.708
and Senator Feinstein.

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:19.245
So this was immediate response.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.180
-You know what's
a little incriminating?

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.116
If you're accused
of sexual assault

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.917
and you just happen
to have on hand

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:27.987
a list of other women
you didn't sexually assault.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.288
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.589
If the cops come to your house

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.358
and say they want to ask you
about a murder,

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.093
and you come to the door
with a list of people

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:36.295
you didn't murder...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:39.131
...you'll still be a suspect
in that murder.

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:40.366
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:42.368
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:45.905
"Every one of these people
is alive."

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:48.808
Alive, alive, alive, alive.

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:51.110
And yet despite the seriousness
of these allegations,

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.545
Republicans
and right-wing pundits

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:54.012
immediately went
on the offensive.

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:56.181
Fox News host Jeanine Pirro,
for example,

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:58.484
attacked California Senator
Dianne Feinstein

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.286
for keeping
the complaint confidential,

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.620
at the woman's request,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:05.257
and implied that she might not
even be a real person.

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.493
-When you get the letter,

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:10.229
what do you do
to make sure it's real?

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:12.932
That the person is even real?

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:15.934
Given the left's penchant
to buy fake dossiers,

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:18.837
make up facts,
and collude with the media

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:22.675
to sabotage even the president
of the United States,

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:27.279
forgive me if I think
it's all hogwash.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:31.317
Why would you wait
to even send it to the FBI?

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:37.322
Is it because nothing in you
and your pack of demon rats --

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:39.791
that's what I said,
demon rats --

00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:45.397
a.k.a. Democrats bag of tricks,
was working against Kavanaugh?

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.233
-Jeanine,
you don't have to clarify

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:48.901
that you said "demon rats."

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.136
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:52.438
You look and sound like a person

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.941
who uses "demon rats"
all the time.

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:56.375
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.811
If your delivery guy
was five minutes late,

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:01.247
I'm pretty sure
you'd call him a demon rat.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:02.248
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:04.583
"When I order my egg rolls..."

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:07.653
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:12.057
"...I want them
when they're hot!"

00:08:12.057 --> 00:08:14.560
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:20.065
Also, you're calling Democrats
demon rats?

00:08:20.065 --> 00:08:23.301
Have you seen the guys
who work in this White House?

00:08:23.301 --> 00:08:26.905
I'm pretty sure Stephen Miller
is a demon who eats rats.

00:08:26.905 --> 00:08:28.407
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:30.375
If you check
the White House fridge,

00:08:30.375 --> 00:08:32.377
his lunch looks like this.

00:08:32.377 --> 00:08:37.249
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:39.385
And then there was Louisiana
Senator John Kennedy,

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:40.920
who was asked
about the allegations

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.389
and chose to complain about
the way Democrats have behaved

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:45.591
throughout Kavanaugh's
confirmation hearings.

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:49.595
-What do you make of this
allegation against Kavanaugh

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.096
back when he was a teenager?

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:52.298
Do you think it'll do anything

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:58.303
to derail his nomination,
his confirmation?

00:08:58.303 --> 00:09:03.642
-I'm fairly confident
that our Founding Fathers

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:06.646
did not intend the process
to work this way.

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:11.684
So far, it's pretty much been
an intergalactic freak show.

00:09:11.684 --> 00:09:14.453
-Excuse me. Have you seen
the guy you voted for?

00:09:14.453 --> 00:09:16.087
Talk about
an intergalactic freak show.

00:09:16.087 --> 00:09:17.423
Trump looks like an extra

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:19.824
from the waiting-room scene
in "Beetlejuice."

00:09:19.824 --> 00:09:22.727
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:22.727 --> 00:09:26.865
Then, yesterday -- yesterday,
the author of the letter,

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:29.000
Christine Blasey Ford,
came forward

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.603
and spoke on the record
to "The Washington Post."

00:09:31.603 --> 00:09:34.106
She provided therapist notes
from 2012

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:35.875
to corroborate her story,
making clear

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:38.377
that the allegations
are, indeed, credible.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.412
And again,
the right tried to discredit her

00:09:40.412 --> 00:09:42.414
or ignore the allegations
altogether.

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:44.150
Republicans on
the Senate Judiciary Committee

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.419
released a statement, calling
them "uncorroborated allegations

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:50.088
from more than 35 years ago,
during high school."

00:09:50.088 --> 00:09:52.291
And when a reporter tracked down
Maine Senator Susan Collins

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:53.692
in the D.C. airport,
she wouldn't say

00:09:53.692 --> 00:09:55.394
if Kavanaugh's hearing
should be delayed.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:57.196
In fact,
she wouldn't even stop walking.

00:09:57.196 --> 00:10:01.500
-Well, I obviously
was very surprised.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:06.806
And, uh, it's -- it's an issue
that I brought up with him

00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:11.777
last Friday, and he denied,

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:14.513
as he did
in his written statement.

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:16.782
That's really all I have
to say at this point.

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:17.983
-What do you think?

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:20.085
should the committee vote
coming up here this week?

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.788
-I'm going to be talking
with my colleagues,

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:26.892
but I really don't have anything
to add at this point.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:29.294
-Do you believe the accuser?

00:10:29.294 --> 00:10:33.699
-I don't know enough to make
a judgment at this point.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.701
-She really covered some ground
in that interview.

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:37.035
[ Laughter ]

00:10:37.035 --> 00:10:38.837
If that was New York,
she would have walked through

00:10:38.837 --> 00:10:40.338
three [bleep] ZIP codes.

00:10:40.338 --> 00:10:44.443
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:44.443 --> 00:10:47.779
Now, Republicans
are really getting desperate

00:10:47.779 --> 00:10:49.281
to avoid reporters.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:53.385
Mitch McConnell actually flies
inside his checked luggage now.

00:10:53.385 --> 00:10:55.253
[ Laughter ]

00:10:55.253 --> 00:10:57.522
And, generally speaking,
when you're running away

00:10:57.522 --> 00:11:00.125
from a reporter asking you about
sexual-assault allegations,

00:11:00.125 --> 00:11:01.560
you're on the wrong side
of history.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.495
And this isn't even
the first entry in this genre.

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:05.864
Last year, Alabama Congressman
Mo Brooks literally

00:11:05.864 --> 00:11:08.534
ran down a flight of stairs
as a reporter chased after him,

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:10.102
asking about the allegations

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:12.304
against Alabama Senate candidate
Roy Moore.

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:28.187
-"Aww, why'd I wear
my tap shoes?!"

00:11:28.187 --> 00:11:29.755
[ Laughter ]

00:11:29.755 --> 00:11:32.258
"Of all the days
to wear my tap shoes."

00:11:32.258 --> 00:11:36.094
[ Applause ]

00:11:36.094 --> 00:11:38.831
Seriously, at this point,
news networks are gonna

